<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_Plant_Wick.xml                     UtinniPatches · SUMP_MECHANICS_1 (S5)
  ============================================================================
  sump_kit_spec.md S5 "the wick-garden crop" (the_sump.md §4 "edge-flora",
  §7 "light as a crop"): "the only living light is farmed fire-in-waiting:
  wick-plants grown in station gardens under no sun at all, harvested as
  candles and lamp-stock." XML-only per the spec's own "no C#" call — pure
  chemotroph pattern on vanilla PlantProperties fields, no new class.

  growMinGlow 0 / growOptimalGlow 1 (explicit, matching the default rather
  than overriding it): SUMP_MECHANICS_1's own spike pass read
  PlantUtility.GrowthRateFactorFor_Light (RimWorld/PlantUtility.cs:361-368) —
  GenMath.InverseLerp(growMinGlow, growOptimalGlow, glow), CLAMPED — and
  confirmed this is "no floor, linear ramp to optimal," not "grows regardless
  of light": growth is proportional to whatever faint ambient glow the
  permanent-dusk biome (RUT_SumpDuskLock + BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension,
  same pass) plus any station lamp light actually provides, and is exactly
  zero only at literal 0.000 glow (HasEnoughLightToGrow, Plant.cs:452). Ban
  #3 ("no sun-driven flora") is satisfied structurally by growMinGlow 0 per
  the kit spec's own field-verified claim (PlantProperties.cs:75, default
  0.51) — this plant needs no sun at all to begin growing, only whatever
  light is present.

  completelyIgnoreFertility true + wildTerrainTags [Water]: the spec's own
  "restricted by terrain affordance to tar-margin terrain grades
  (LIQUID_TYPES_MOD_1 names them)" clause, engine-mapped this pass.
  PlantProperties has NO terrainAffordanceNeeded-style field (that field
  exists on ThingDef generally but GenConstruct.cs:494/653/658 only ever
  checks it for ThingCategory.Building — confirmed this pass, not assumed) —
  the real vanilla mechanism for restricting a SOWN/wild plant to specific
  terrain is PlantUtility.CanEverPlantAt's wildTerrainTags overlap check
  (RimWorld/PlantUtility.cs:140, `WildTerrainTags.Overlaps(terrain.tags)`),
  which also gates player sowing, not only wild spread (same function feeds
  both routes). RM_TarShallow / RM_TarDeep (src/RimMandrake/FlowWorks/Defs/LiquidTypes/
  Defs/TerrainDefs/RM_Tar.xml, LIQUID_TYPES_MOD_1's own generated file, read
  not edited this pass) both carry the vanilla `Water` tag inherited from
  WaterBase, and no other terrain the Sump biome can generate carries it
  (ban #4 — no vanilla water TerrainDef in this biome's own mapping) — so
  `wildTerrainTags: [Water]` is, in the Sump's own context, exactly "the tar
  grades." completelyIgnoreFertility is required alongside it: WaterBase
  itself sets `fertility 0` (Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml:6,
  confirmed against the live install this pass), which would otherwise
  refuse ANY plant outright (PlantUtility.cs:85, fertilityMin default 0.9)
  regardless of the terrain-tag match — thematically apt too: a chemotroph
  "feeding directly on the tar's energy rather than the sun" (§4) has no
  business being fertility-gated by soil chemistry at all.
  GrowthRateFactorFor_Fertility (PlantUtility.cs:352-358) also returns a flat
  1.0 once this flag is set, so the plant pays no growth penalty for it
  either. Wild-growth inside a Building_PlantGrower (station hydroponics-
  style planter) bypasses the wildTerrainTags check entirely per the same
  function (the `!flag` guard, PlantUtility.cs:138) — consistent with "grown
  in station gardens": a planter box works regardless of the terrain under
  it, exactly like vanilla hydroponics crops.

  minGrowthTemperature -8: sump_kit_spec.md S5's own INVENTED value
  ("growMinTemp lowered for the cold... sheet §0 temps straddle freezing").
  the_sump.md §0's own measured range (p10/median/p90 -4.3/1.2/14.9 degC)
  sits mostly above -8, so the crop can grow through ordinary Sump cold
  without artificial heating; other temperature fields (minOptimal/
  maxOptimal/maxGrowthTemperature) left at PlantBaseNonEdible's inherited
  defaults — the spec names no figure for them, not invented here.

  Texture reused from vanilla (Things/Plant/Ambrosia — a real, confirmed
  texPath, Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/Plants_Special.xml:118) rather than
  commissioning new art, same practice as RUT_TwinkleSpikeTestPlant.xml in
  this same mod: this pass proves the mechanism, not the final look. Art
  pass owed.

  growDays/harvestYield/harvestWork/sowWork/statBases: this pass's own
  INVENTED-BUILD values (moderate, station-garden-crop scale), not named by
  the kit spec beyond growMinGlow/growMinTemp. High Flammability (2.0) is
  deliberate — this plant IS candle-stock; RUT_WickStem (ThingDefs_Items/,
  same pass) is the harvested fuel good.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBaseNonEdible">
    <defName>RUT_Plant_Wick</defName>
    <label>wick-plant</label>
    <description>A low, waxy stand of stems that feeds directly on the tar's own chemistry rather than the sun — it needs no daylight at all, only whatever faint light is already there. Junker stations cultivate it in wick-gardens at the tar's edge; harvested and dried, its stems are the only living light the Sump ever gives back.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/Ambrosia</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>2.0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <growMinGlow>0</growMinGlow>
      <growOptimalGlow>1</growOptimalGlow>
      <completelyIgnoreFertility>true</completelyIgnoreFertility>
      <wildTerrainTags>
        <li>Water</li>
      </wildTerrainTags>
      <minGrowthTemperature>-8</minGrowthTemperature>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <sowTags>
        <li>Ground</li>
        <li>Hydroponic</li>
      </sowTags>
      <sowWork>170</sowWork>
      <harvestWork>180</harvestWork>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <harvestedThingDef>RUT_WickStem</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>6</harvestYield>
      <growDays>6</growDays>
      <visualSizeRange>0.6~1.05</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.15</topWindExposure>
      <wildOrder>2</wildOrder>
      <purpose>Misc</purpose>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
